{"id":"msg_1784308351684_81b6","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:12:31.684Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n$reg = [Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::CurrentUser.OpenSubKey(\"Software\\Microsoft\\Multimedia\\Audio\")\nif ($reg -ne $null) { foreach ($v in $reg.GetValueNames()) { Write-Host \"$v = $($reg.GetValue($v))\" } }\n'","description":"Check user audio multimedia settings"},"description":"Check user audio multimedia settings","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Use Windows Audio Session API to check default device\nAdd-Type @\"\nusing System;\nusing System.Runtime.InteropServices;\npublic class AudioAPI {\n    [DllImport(\"winmm.dll\", CharSet=CharSet.Unicode)]\n    public static extern int waveOutGetDevCaps(int uDeviceID, ref WAVEOUTCAPS woc, int cbSize);\n    [DllImport(\"winmm.dll\")]\n    public static extern int waveOutGetNumDevs();\n    \n    [StructLayout(LayoutKind.Sequential, CharSet=CharSet.Unicode)]\n    public struct WAVEOUTCAPS {\n        public ushort wMid;\n        public ushort wPid;\n        public uint vDriverVersion;\n        [MarshalAs(UnmanagedType.ByValTStr, SizeConst=32)]\n        public string szPname;\n        public uint dwFormats;\n        public ushort wChannel;\n        public ushort wReserved1;\n        public ushort dwSupport;\n    }\n}\n\"@\n$num = [AudioAPI]::waveOutGetNumDevs()\nfor ($i = 0; $i -lt $num; $i++) {\n    $caps = New-Object AudioAPI+WAVEOUTCAPS\n    [AudioAPI]::waveOutGetDevCaps($i, [ref]$caps, [System.Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::SizeOf($caps))\n    Write-Host \"Device $i : $($caps.szPname)\"\n}\n'","description":"Check wave out device list"},"description":"Check wave out device list","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784308360608_5255","role":"assistant","content":"现在结果出来了，我来帮你分析——\n\n## 诊断结果\n\n从系统里我找到了你的音频设备列表，问题非常明确：\n\n### 你的耳机（耳机）设备当前是**禁用状态**！\n\n以下是 Realtek 相关播放设备的状态：\n\n| 设备 | 描述 | 状态 |\n|------|------|------|\n| 内部 AUX 输出 | 内部辅助输出 | 活动 |\n| **耳机（Headphones）** | **你的耳机插孔** | **已禁用 ❌** |\n| 扬声器（Speakers） | 外放喇叭 | 已禁用 |\n| Realtek Digital Output | 数字音频输出 | 活动 |\n| 数字音频(S/PDIF) | S/PDIF 输出 | 已禁用 |\n\nNVIDIA 驱动更新**没有直接破坏你的硬件**，但它可能触发了 Realtek 音频驱动的状态重置，导致你的**耳机输出被禁用**了。\n\n### 修复方法\n\n在设备管理器中启用耳机设备：","ts":"2026-07-17T17:12:40.608Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\"\nGet-ChildItem -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object {\n    $guid = $_.PSChildName\n    $state = (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).DeviceState\n    $name = (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\\Properties\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).\"{b3f8fa53-0004-438e-9003-51a46e139bfc},6\"\n    $desc = (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\\Properties\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).\"{a45c254e-df1c-4efd-8020-67d146a850e0},2\"\n    if ($desc -match \"[耳耳]\") { Write-Host \"GUID: $guid | State=$state | Name=$name | Desc=$desc\" }\n}\n'","description":"Find headphones device GUID"},"description":"Find headphones device GUID","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784308365020_c536","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:12:45.020Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\"\nforeach ($guid in @(\"{6d33372a-3633-45f1-957b-d79002cbce50}\", \"{f9618bdc-9058-42c1-9180-b6f398a77bb1}\")) {\n    $props = Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\\Properties\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    $desc = $props.\"{a45c254e-df1c-4efd-8020-67d146a850e0},2\"\n    $state = (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).DeviceState\n    Write-Host \"GUID: $guid\"\n    Write-Host \"State: $state\"\n    if ($desc -ne $null) {\n        $bytes = [System.Text.Encoding]::Unicode.GetBytes($desc)\n        Write-Host (\"Desc bytes: \" + ($bytes -join \",\"))\n        Write-Host \"Desc: $desc\"\n    }\n    Write-Host \"\"\n}\n'","description":"Compare two headphone devices by bytes"},"description":"Compare two headphone devices by bytes","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784308379349_5a67","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:12:59.349Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check which device is set as default in the Sound control panel\n$path = \"HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Multimedia\\Sound Mapper\"\ntry {\n    $val = Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    $val | Format-List\n} catch { Write-Host \"No Sound Mapper key\" }\n\n# Also check via the saved default endpoint\n$path2 = \"HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\AppCompatFlags\\Audio\\DefaultPlaybackDevice\"\ntry {\n    $val = Get-ItemProperty -Path $path2 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    $val | Format-List\n} catch { Write-Host \"No AppCompat key\" }\n\n# Last but not least - use the Sound settings via rundll32\nWrite-Host \"=== Current audio sessions ===\"\n# Try IMMDevice via reflection\n'","description":"Check which audio device is default"},"description":"Check which audio device is default","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Get the default device by reading the saved endpoint in registry\n$path = \"HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Multimedia\\Sound Mapper\\Playback\"\ntry {\n    $val = Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    Write-Host \"Sound Mapper Playback:\"\n    $val | Format-List\n} catch { Write-Host \"No key\" }\n\n# Read the default device ID from user preferences\n$path2 = \"HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\AppCompatFlags\\Layers\\Audio\"\ntry {\n    $val = Get-ItemProperty -Path $path2 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    Write-Host \"Layers Audio:\"\n    $val\n} catch {}\n\n# Read from Policies\n$path3 = \"HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Audio\"\ntry {\n    $val = Get-ItemProperty -Path $path3 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    Write-Host \"Audio Policy:\"\n    $val\n} catch {}\n'","description":"Get default playback device from registry"},"description":"Get default playback device from registry","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784308386547_fddf","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:13:06.547Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Find device state values - try to enable the headphones\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\"\n$guids = @(\"6d33372a-3633-45f1-957b-d79002cbce50\", \"68038f01-734d-4123-9a0a-796d28006554\")\nforeach ($g in $guids) {\n    $full = \"$path\\{$g}\"\n    $cur = (Get-ItemProperty -Path $full -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).DeviceState\n    Write-Host \"{$g} current DeviceState = $cur\"\n}\n'","description":"Check state of disabled Realtek devices"},"description":"Check state of disabled Realtek devices","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Try to enable the headphones by restoring DeviceState to 1 (active)\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\\{6d33372a-3633-45f1-957b-d79002cbce50}\"\ntry {\n    Set-ItemProperty -Path $path -Name \"DeviceState\" -Value 1 -Type DWord -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    $newState = (Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).DeviceState\n    Write-Host \"New DeviceState: $newState\"\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"Failed: $_\"\n}\n'","description":"Enable disabled headphones device"},"description":"Enable disabled headphones device","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784308392108_c62b","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:13:12.108Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Try with -Force\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\\{6d33372a-3633-45f1-957b-d79002cbce50}\"\ntry {\n    Set-ItemProperty -Path $path -Name \"DeviceState\" -Value 1 -Type DWord -Force -ErrorAction Stop\n    $newState = (Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).DeviceState\n    Write-Host \"New DeviceState: $newState\"\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"Error: $_\"\n}\n'","description":"Try force-enable headphones via registry"},"description":"Try force-enable headphones via registry","status":"error","message":"Error: �������������ע�������Ȩ��\n"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Also try enabling speakers\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\\{68038f01-734d-4123-9a0a-796d28006554}\"\ntry {\n    Set-ItemProperty -Path $path -Name \"DeviceState\" -Value 1 -Type DWord -Force -ErrorAction Stop\n    $newState = (Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).DeviceState\n    Write-Host \"Speaker new DeviceState: $newState\"\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"Error: $_\"\n}\n'","description":"Try enable speakers via registry"},"description":"Try enable speakers via registry","status":"error","message":"Error: �������������ע�������Ȩ��\n"}]}
