{"id":"msg_1784310201004_c8a9","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:43:21.004Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check for any audio enhancements/effects that might be blocking output\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Audio\"\nGet-ChildItem -Path \"$path\\Effects\\Render\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object {\n    Write-Host \"Effect: $($_.PSChildName)\"\n    Get-ItemProperty -Path $_.PSPath -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Out-String\n}\n'","description":"Check audio effect chain"},"description":"Check audio effect chain","status":"error","message":"Exit code 1\n"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Try to generate a simple beep sound via the PC speaker and via audio API\n# First check if the system speaker works\n[System.Console]::Beep(1000, 200) 2>&1\nWrite-Host \"Console.Beep executed (may use internal speaker)\"\n'","description":"Test system beep"},"description":"Test system beep","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check all properties of the speakers to see if the format string is stored\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\\{f9618bdc-9058-42c1-9180-b6f398a77bb1}\\Properties\"\n$props = Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n$props.PSObject.Properties | Where-Object { $_.Name -like \"*b3f8fa53*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*format*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*Format*\" } | ForEach-Object {\n    Write-Host \"$($_.Name) = $($_.Value)\"\n}\n'","description":"Check all audio format entries in registry"},"description":"Check all audio format entries in registry","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310217478_9b13","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:43:37.478Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check what driver is actually controlling the Realtek device\n$drv = Get-CimInstance Win32_PnPSignedDriver | Where-Object { $_.DeviceName -eq \"Realtek High Definition Audio\" } | Select-Object DeviceName,DriverVersion,DriverDate,DriverProviderName,InfName,IsSigned\n$drv | Format-List\n\n# Check the INF file\n$infPath = \"$env:SystemRoot\\System32\\DriverStore\\FileRepository\\oem11.inf_amd64_*\" 2>$null\nGet-ChildItem $infPath -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object FullName\n'","description":"Check Realtek driver INF details"},"description":"Check Realtek driver INF details","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Try to play a sound via .NET SoundPlayer\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms\ntry {\n    # Generate a simple WAV in memory - a 440Hz sine wave for 1 second\n    $sampleRate = 22050\n    $duration = 0.5\n    $numSamples = [int]($sampleRate * $duration)\n    $bitsPerSample = 16\n    $numChannels = 1\n    \n    $ms = New-Object System.IO.MemoryStream\n    $writer = New-Object System.IO.BinaryWriter($ms)\n    \n    # RIFF header\n    $writer.Write([char[]]\"RIFF\")\n    $fileSize = 36 + $numSamples * 2\n    $writer.Write([int]$fileSize)\n    $writer.Write([char[]]\"WAVE\")\n    \n    # fmt chunk\n    $writer.Write([char[]]\"fmt \")\n    $writer.Write([int]16)\n    $writer.Write([short]1)  # PCM\n    $writer.Write([short]$numChannels)\n    $writer.Write([int]$sampleRate)\n    $writer.Write([int]($sampleRate * $numChannels * $bitsPerSample / 8))\n    $writer.Write([short]($numChannels * $bitsPerSample / 8))\n    $writer.Write([short]$bitsPerSample)\n    \n    # data chunk\n    $writer.Write([char[]]\"data\")\n    $dataSize = $numSamples * 2\n    $writer.Write([int]$dataSize)\n    \n    for ($i = 0; $i -lt $numSamples; $i++) {\n        $sample = [int]([Math]::Sin(2 * [Math]::PI * 440 * $i / $sampleRate) * 16000)\n        $writer.Write([short]$sample)\n    }\n    \n    $writer.Flush()\n    $ms.Position = 0\n    \n    $player = New-Object System.Media.SoundPlayer($ms)\n    $player.PlaySync()\n    Write-Host \"Sound played successfully\"\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"Error playing sound: $_\"\n}\n'","description":"Try to play test sound via .NET","timeout":15000},"description":"Try to play test sound via .NET","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310226346_5694","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:43:46.346Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Try to play a simple sound using .NET\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms\ntry {\n    $sampleRate = 22050\n    $duration = 0.5\n    $numSamples = $sampleRate * $duration\n    \n    $ms = New-Object System.IO.MemoryStream\n    $writer = New-Object System.IO.BinaryWriter($ms)\n    \n    # RIFF header\n    $writer.Write([Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetBytes(\"RIFF\"))\n    $fileSize = 36 + $numSamples * 2\n    $writer.Write($fileSize)\n    $writer.Write([Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetBytes(\"WAVE\"))\n    \n    # fmt chunk\n    $writer.Write([Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetBytes(\"fmt \"))\n    $writer.Write(16)   # chunk size\n    $writer.Write([UInt16]1)   # PCM\n    $writer.Write([UInt16]1)   # mono\n    $writer.Write($sampleRate)\n    $writer.Write($sampleRate * 2)   # byte rate\n    $writer.Write([UInt16]2)   # block align\n    $writer.Write([UInt16]16)  # bits per sample\n    \n    # data chunk\n    $writer.Write([Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetBytes(\"data\"))\n    $dataSize = $numSamples * 2\n    $writer.Write($dataSize)\n    \n    for ($i = 0; $i -lt $numSamples; $i++) {\n        $sample = [Math]::Sin(2 * [Math]::PI * 440 * $i / $sampleRate) * 16000\n        $writer.Write([UInt16][Math]::Max(0, [Math]::Min(65535, $sample + 32768)))\n    }\n    \n    $writer.Flush()\n    $ms.Position = 0\n    \n    $player = New-Object System.Media.SoundPlayer($ms)\n    Write-Host \"Attempting to play sound...\"\n    $player.PlaySync()\n    Write-Host \"Sound played successfully!\"\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"Error: $_\"\n    Write-Host \"Exception type: $($_.Exception.GetType().Name)\"\n}\n'","description":"Play test sound via .NET SoundPlayer","timeout":15000},"description":"Play test sound via .NET SoundPlayer","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310237541_d8e8","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:43:57.542Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Try using Text-to-Speech to test audio output\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName System.Speech\ntry {\n    $synth = New-Object System.Speech.Synthesis.SpeechSynthesizer\n    Write-Host \"TTS device: $($synth.Voice.Name)\"\n    $synth.Speak(\"test audio\")\n    Write-Host \"TTS spoke successfully\"\n}\ncatch {\n    Write-Host \"TTS Error: $_\"\n}\n'","description":"Test audio via Speech API","timeout":15000},"description":"Test audio via Speech API","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check the SndVol settings (volume mixer)\n$path = \"HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\LowRegistry\\Audio\\PolicyConfig\\SoundMixer\"\ntry {\n    Get-ChildItem -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object {\n        Write-Host \"--- Mixer: $($_.PSChildName) ---\"\n        Get-ItemProperty -Path $_.PSPath -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Out-String\n    }\n} catch { Write-Host \"No mixer settings\" }\n' 2>&1 | head -50","description":"Check volume mixer settings"},"description":"Check volume mixer settings","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310247050_4a4a","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:44:07.050Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Try playing a system sound\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName System.Media\ntry {\n    [System.Media.SystemSounds]::Asterisk.Play()\n    Write-Host \"System sound played\"\n    Start-Sleep -Seconds 1\n    [System.Media.SystemSounds]::Beep.Play()\n    Write-Host \"Beep played\"\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"Error: $_\"\n}\n\n# Also check Windows version\n[System.Environment]::OSVersion.Version\n'","description":"Test system sounds","timeout":10000},"description":"Test system sounds","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Use SpeechSynthesizer to speak, but force it to use specific device\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName System.Speech\ntry {\n    $synth = New-Object System.Speech.Synthesis.SpeechSynthesizer\n    $devices = @($synth.GetInstalledVoices())\n    Write-Host \"Available voices:\"\n    foreach ($v in $devices) {\n        Write-Host \"  $($v.VoiceInfo.Name) - $($v.VoiceInfo.Description)\"\n    }\n    # Get output device info\n    Write-Host \"Output audio device: $($synth.State)\"\n}\ncatch {\n    Write-Host \"Error: $_\"\n}\n'","description":"Check TTS voice details"},"description":"Check TTS voice details","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310260434_42f7","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:44:20.434Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check Windows version more specifically\nGet-ItemProperty \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\" -Name ProductName,ReleaseId,CurrentBuild,DisplayVersion | Format-List\n'","description":"Get exact Windows version"},"description":"Get exact Windows version","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check Realtek audio device for jack detection info\n# Look for jack-related properties\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\\{f9618bdc-9058-42c1-9180-b6f398a77bb1}\\Properties\"\n$props = Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n$props.PSObject.Properties | Where-Object { $_.Name -like \"*jack*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*Jack*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*plug*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*Plug*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*connect*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*Connect*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*detect*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*Detect*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*e4870e26*\" } | ForEach-Object {\n    Write-Host \"$($_.Name) = $($_.Value)\"\n}\nWrite-Host \"---\"\n# Also check for KS (Kernel Streaming) properties\n$props.PSObject.Properties | Where-Object { $_.Name -like \"*e4870e26*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*83da6326*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*1da5d803*\" -or $_.Name -like \"*233164c8*\" } | ForEach-Object {\n    Write-Host \"$($_.Name) = $($_.Value)\"\n}\n'","description":"Check jack detection configuration"},"description":"Check jack detection configuration","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310278398_1cd2","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:44:38.398Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check the Kernel Streaming pin for each Realtek render endpoint\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\"\nGet-ChildItem -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object {\n    $guid = $_.PSChildName\n    $name = (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\\Properties\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).\"{b3f8fa53-0004-438e-9003-51a46e139bfc},6\"\n    $desc = (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\\Properties\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).\"{a45c254e-df1c-4efd-8020-67d146a850e0},2\"\n    $state = (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).DeviceState\n    $kspin = (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\\Properties\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).\"{233164c8-1b2c-4c7d-bc68-b671687a2567},1\"\n    $pintype = (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$path\\$guid\\Properties\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).\"{e4870e26-3cc5-4cd2-ba46-ca0a9a70ed04},0\"\n    if ($name -like \"*Realtek*\" -or $name -like \"*High Definition*\") {\n        Write-Host \"GUID=$guid\"\n        Write-Host \"  Name=$name\"\n        Write-Host \"  Desc=$desc\"\n        Write-Host \"  State=$state\"\n        if ($kspin) { Write-Host \"  KS Pin=$kspin\" }\n        Write-Host \"\"\n    }\n}\n'","description":"Check KS pin info for all Realtek endpoints"},"description":"Check KS pin info for all Realtek endpoints","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310289858_5c41","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:44:49.858Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Realtek APO settings - often stored in these locations\n$paths = @(\n    \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Realtek\",\n    \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Realtek Semiconductor Corp.\",\n    \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\WOW6432Node\\Realtek\",\n    \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\WOW6432Node\\Realtek Semiconductor Corp.\",\n    \"HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\IntcAzAudAddService\",\n    \"HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\RtkAudio*\",\n    \"HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Class\\{4d36e96c-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\"\n)\nforeach ($p in $paths) {\n    if (Test-Path $p) {\n        Write-Host \"=== Found: $p ===\"\n        Get-ItemProperty -Path $p -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Out-String\n    }\n}\n' 2>&1","description":"Check Realtek APO and driver settings"},"description":"Check Realtek APO and driver settings","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310295646_08e9","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:44:55.646Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\nGet-Service -Name \"IntcAzAudAddService\" | Format-List Name,DisplayName,Status,StartType\n'","description":"Check Realtek audio service status"},"description":"Check Realtek audio service status","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check audio class settings for the specific Realtek device\n$classPath = \"HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Class\\{4d36e96c-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\"\nGet-ChildItem -Path $classPath -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Where-Object { $_.PSChildName -match \"^[0-9a-f]{4}$\" } | ForEach-Object {\n    $prop = Get-ItemProperty -Path $_.PSPath -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    $inf = $prop.InfSection\n    $desc = $prop.DriverDesc\n    $mfg = $prop.Mfg\n    $hwid = $prop.HardwareID -join \",\"\n    if ($desc -like \"*Realtek*\" -or $desc -like \"*NVIDIA*\" -or $desc -like \"*High Definition*\") {\n        Write-Host \"Key: $($_.PSChildName)\"\n        Write-Host \"  DriverDesc: $desc\"\n        Write-Host \"  Mfg: $mfg\"\n        Write-Host \"  InfSection: $inf\"\n        Write-Host \"  HWID: $hwid\"\n        Write-Host \"  DriverDate: $($prop.DriverDate)\"\n        Write-Host \"  DriverVersion: $($prop.DriverVersion)\"\n        Write-Host \"\"\n    }\n}\n'","description":"Check audio class driver details"},"description":"Check audio class driver details","status":"error","message":"Exit code 1\nKey: 0000\n  DriverDesc: NVIDIA High Definition Audio\n  Mfg: \n  InfSection: WINBLUENVHDA64V\n  HWID: \n  DriverDate: 8-14-2024\n  DriverVersion: 1.4.0.1\n\nKey: 0001\n  DriverDesc: Realtek High Definition Audio\n  Mfg: \n  InfSection: IntcAzAudModel.NTamd64\n  HWID: \n  DriverDate: 9-16-2025\n  DriverVersion: 6.0.9888.1\n\nKey: 0008\n  DriverDesc: NVIDIA Virtual Audio Device (Wave Extensible) (WDM)\n  Mfg: \n  InfSection: NVVAD_WaveExtensible64.NT\n  HWID: \n  DriverDate: 5-13-2025\n  DriverVersion: 4.65.0.12\n\n"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310306956_bf99","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:45:06.956Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check audio enhancements setting for the speakers device\n$path = \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\MMDevices\\Audio\\Render\\{f9618bdc-9058-42c1-9180-b6f398a77bb1}\\FxProperties\"\nif (Test-Path $path) {\n    Write-Host \"FxProperties exists (audio enhancements may be active)\"\n    Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Out-String\n} else {\n    Write-Host \"No FxProperties (audio enhancements not configured)\"\n}\n\n# Check for APO registration\n$path2 = \"HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Class\\{4d36e96c-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\0001\\Global\"\nif (Test-Path $path2) {\n    Write-Host \"Global APO settings:\"\n    Get-ItemProperty -Path $path2 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Out-String\n} else {\n    Write-Host \"No Global APO key for device 0001\"\n} \n\n# Check for the APO subkey\n$path3 = \"HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Class\\{4d36e96c-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\0001\"\nGet-ChildItem -Path $path3 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object { \n    Write-Host \"SubKey: $($_.PSChildName)\" \n}\n'","description":"Check audio enhancements and APO"},"description":"Check audio enhancements and APO","status":"success"},{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check communications settings\n$path = \"HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Multimedia\\Audio\"\ntry {\n    $val = Get-ItemProperty -Path $path -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n    Write-Host \"Audio Multimedia settings:\"\n    $val.PSObject.Properties | Where-Object { $_.Name -notlike \"PS*\" } | ForEach-Object {\n        Write-Host \"  $($_.Name) = $($_.Value)\"\n    }\n} catch {}\n'","description":"Check Windows communications audio settings"},"description":"Check Windows communications audio settings","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310311187_48d0","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:45:11.187Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n$base = \"HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Class\\{4d36e96c-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\0001\"\n\n# Check Settings\n$settings = Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$base\\Settings\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\nWrite-Host \"=== Settings ===\"\n$settings.PSObject.Properties | Where-Object { $_.Name -notlike \"PS*\" } | ForEach-Object {\n    Write-Host \"  $($_.Name) = $($_.Value)\"\n}\n\n# Check GlobalSettings\n$gs = Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$base\\GlobalSettings\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\nWrite-Host \"=== GlobalSettings ===\"\n$gs.PSObject.Properties | Where-Object { $_.Name -notlike \"PS*\" } | ForEach-Object {\n    Write-Host \"  $($_.Name) = $($_.Value)\"\n}\n\n# Check PinConfigOverrideVerbs\n$pin = Get-ItemProperty -Path \"$base\\PinConfigOverrideVerbs\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\nWrite-Host \"=== PinConfigOverrideVerbs ===\"\n$pin.PSObject.Properties | Where-Object { $_.Name -notlike \"PS*\" } | ForEach-Object {\n    Write-Host \"  $($_.Name) = $($_.Value)\"\n}\n' 2>&1","description":"Check Realtek driver configuration settings"},"description":"Check Realtek driver configuration settings","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310329862_8a3a","role":"assistant","content":"","ts":"2026-07-17T17:45:29.862Z","toolCalls":[{"name":"Bash","args":{"command":"powershell -Command '\n# Check for ASUS motherboard model\nGet-CimInstance Win32_BaseBoard | Select-Object Manufacturer,Product\n\n# Check BIOS version\nGet-CimInstance Win32_BIOS | Select-Object Manufacturer,SMBIOSBIOSVersion,ReleaseDate\n'","description":"Check motherboard model"},"description":"Check motherboard model","status":"success"}]}
{"id":"msg_1784310339533_31da","role":"assistant","content":"好的，我已经做了全面的诊断。你的机器是 **ASUS PRIME Z370-P** 主板，搭载 **Realtek ALC887** 声卡。以下是完整诊断和解决方案：\n\n---\n\n## 诊断结论\n\n从系统层面看，音频链路一切正常：\n\n| 检查项 | 结果 |\n|--------|------|\n| 默认设备 | 喇叭 (Realtek) — **已启用** |\n| Realtek 驱动 | 6.0.9888.1 (2025/9/16) — 正常 |\n| IntcAzAudAddService | Running |\n| 音频服务 | Audiosrv / AudioEndpointBuilder — 正常 |\n| 耳机设备 | **已禁用** (State=4) |\n| 音量级别 | Level = 32 (正常) |\n\n但关键信息：.NET SoundPlayer 直接播放报 **\"句柄无效\"错误**，说明音频数据无法真正到达硬件。\n\n---\n\n## 解决方法（按顺序试）\n\n### 方法一：更改音频格式（最快，成功率最高）\n\n1. 右键任务栏喇叭图标 → **声音(Sound)**\n2. **播放(Playback)** 选项卡 → 双击 **喇叭(Speakers) Realtek High Definition Audio**\n3. 点 **高级(Advanced)** 选项卡\n4. 在 **默认格式(Default Format)** 里，改成 **16 bit, 44100 Hz (CD音质)**\n5. 点 **测试(Test)**，然后点确定\n\n### 方法二：启用耳机设备\n\n1. 同样在 **声音 → 播放** 页面\n2. 右键空白处 → 勾选 **显示禁用的设备(Show Disabled Devices)**\n3. 会看到灰色显示的 **耳机(Headphones)** → 右键 **启用(Enable)**\n4. 再把耳机设为默认设备试试有没有声音\n\n### 方法三：卸载 NVIDIA HD Audio 驱动\n\n之前禁用了 NVIDIA HD Audio 但驱动还在系统里，需要彻底卸载：\n\n1. **Win+X → 设备管理器**\n2. **声音、视频和游戏控制器** → 找到所有 **NVIDIA High Definition Audio**\n3. 右键 → **卸载设备**（勾选\"删除此设备的驱动程序软件\"）\n4. 完成后 **重启电脑**\n\n### 方法四：重装 Realtek 驱动（回退到微软通用驱动）\n\n这个是针对 Realtek UAD 驱动与 NVIDIA 驱动冲突的终极手段：\n\n1. 设备管理器 → **Realtek High Definition Audio** → 右键 **卸载设备**\n2. **勾选\"删除此设备的驱动程序软件\"**\n3. 重启电脑\n4. 重启后 Windows 会自动安装微软自带的 **High Definition Audio Device**（通用驱动）\n5. 如果这时有声音了，就是 Realtek UAD 驱动的问题\n\n> 如果通用驱动有声音但功能不全，可以再从 ASUS 官网下载对应主板的 Realtek 驱动重装。\n\n### 方法五：系统文件检查\n\n以管理员身份运行 CMD：\n```cmd\nsfc /scannow\n```\n\n---\n\n你先从 **方法一**（改音频格式为 16bit 44100Hz）开始试，这是最常见的\"驱动更新后无声\"的解决方案。如果不行再依次试后面的方法。","ts":"2026-07-17T17:45:39.533Z"}
